---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProblemsNav from '../../components/problems/ProblemsNav.astro';
---

<Base
  title="ROCm bug report template"
  description="Template and collect-rocm-report.sh for filing useful ROCm / llama.cpp / Ollama bugs."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <ProblemsNav current="report" />
    <h1 class="display mt-6 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Write a good bug report</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      A useful report is boring: versions, the exact command, the first error, and whether
      a published workaround changed anything. No tok/s you did not measure.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-lab prose mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2 id="script">Collect versions</h2>
      <p>
        Download
        <a href="/rocm-problems/collect-rocm-report.sh"><code>collect-rocm-report.sh</code></a>
        and run it on the box that fails:
      </p>
      <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://amdai.net/rocm-problems/collect-rocm-report.sh -o collect-rocm-report.sh
chmod +x collect-rocm-report.sh
./collect-rocm-report.sh | tee rocm-report.txt</code></pre>
      <p>
        The script prints OS (without hostname), amdgpu/kfd, rocminfo lines that are not
        UUIDs, hipconfig, amd-smi or rocm-smi, optional clinfo, and the env vars people
        actually set (<code>HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION</code>, device isolation). Read the
        file before you paste. It does not upload anything.
      </p>

      <h2 id="template">Template</h2>
      <pre><code>## What I expected
Tokens on the discrete GPU (gfx ID: ____).

## What happened
Paste the first error, not a paraphrase.

## Hardware
- GPU / gfx:
- OS / distro / kernel:
- ROCm / HIP prefix:
- Backend + version (llama.cpp / Strata / vLLM / Ollama):
- Model / quant / context (Q3+; Q1/Q2 stay off):

## Command
```
# exact argv
```

## Already tried
- [ ] llama.cpp Vulkan on the same GGUF
- [ ] Unset HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION
- [ ] One GPU visible (HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES / GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES)
- [ ] Matching thread: (AMDai tracker URL or GitHub issue)

## Logs
Attach `rocm-report.txt` and `dmesg | grep -iE 'amdgpu|MODE1|MES'` if it hung.
</code></pre>

      <h2 id="where">Where to file</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Driver / runtime / HIP: <a href="https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues">ROCm/ROCm issues</a></li>
        <li>llama.cpp: <a href="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues">ggml-org/llama.cpp</a></li>
        <li>vLLM: <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues">vllm-project/vllm</a></li>
        <li>Ollama: <a href="https://github.com/ollama/ollama/issues">ollama/ollama</a></li>
        <li>PyTorch: <a href="https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues">pytorch/pytorch</a></li>
        <li>Home-lab discussion with a rig badge: <a href="/forum/new?category=install-drivers">Ask the forum</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Search the <a href="/rocm-problems">tracker</a> and the upstream issue first.
        If it matches, add repro data there. See <a href="/rocm-problems/help">how you can help</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
